{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Runs a saved FLOW command once - an ORDINARY run, not a debug session - and reports which root cases of its nextcase chain ran. R5: a thin wrapper over dev.flowstep.run_flow (flowlang's own stepper, the semantics Command::execute runs; no debug session, no tape, no 10k debugger budget, no sentinel nextcase). Returns {status, result, path, cases} plus complete, outcome, end, steps, max_depth, budget, ms, us. result is the envelope a plain run returns (app.app.exec's auth check and format_result; a root terminate is success with the output delivered so far; a failure is {status err, msg, flow_end}). path is [{case, end, op?, ms, us, steps}], one per ROOT case executed, root first, always COMPLETE (nested frames never enter it); end is next (a next rule fired; op = the op), done, terminate, fail, stall, I-4, panic, or budget. ms/us are real monotonic wall time per case measured at the run boundary (nested work is attributed to the root case it ran under). Step budget = the ordinary run's 1,000,000 steps; running out is an explicit budget error (result.flow_end budget). Runs the SAVED body. Inputs: lib, ctl, cmd name the flow command; args are its arguments (JSONObject); nn_sessionid is filled in by the framework (pass \"\" from javascript). Admin-only.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"name":"args","type":"JSONObject"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"msuuqu1a165e00598r1161","readers":[],"time":1793453039441,"username":"system","writers":[]}